# motion-design-taste

The aesthetic and motion-language layer that sits **above** the GSAP API skills. Apply at the START of any task that produces an animated frontend interface, before writing GSAP code.

Output a one-line **Design Read** before any code:
> "Reading this as: \<page kind\> for \<audience\>, with a \<vibe\> language, leaning toward \<aesthetic family\> and \<motion language\>."

Then set three dials (`MOTION_INTENSITY`, `DESIGN_VARIANCE`, `VISUAL_DENSITY` — each 1-10), pick a motion mode (Restrained / Expressive / Cinematic), and route to the right API skill.

Avoid LLM defaults: `Inter` everywhere, AI-purple gradients on dark mesh, centered hero with H1 over a glowing radial blur, `back.out` / `elastic.*` as default ease, parallax on every section.

For full guidance, three dials, motion modes, decision table, and Lila Rule: see `skills/motion-design-taste/SKILL.md`.
